  "id": "perceptualization",
  "term": "perceptualization",
  "definition": "Perceptualization is the shaping of information into a perceptible form, especially in art or visualization, so it can influence how people understand and feel about it. In this source, it refers to more than simply converting facts into images, because its effect depends on how factual and invented elements are combined.",
